  "description": "NOAA AOML Seascapes: a global biogeographic framework in which space and time are classified simultaneously from synoptic satellite time series using hierarchical, topology-preserving machine learning. 8-day composites on a 0.05 degree global grid; CLASS is a categorical seascape label (1-33) and P is the associated probability. Upstream at NOAA AOML CoastWatch (cwcgom.aoml.noaa.gov); re-served with CORS and Parquet by erddap.oceanmetrics.io, and referenced in place for computing place statistics in the browser via griddap.parquet.",
